# Koh, the Face Stealer (CR 607.2a, 607.2d, 400.7, 613.1f): Koh's enters trigger exiles Bot1's own Chrome Companion and Bot1 pays 1
# life to choose it. On turn 4 Bot2's Binding Negotiation puts that face-up exiled card into Bot1's graveyard: it is a new object
# there, not "the last chosen card" that is exiled with Koh, so on turn 5 Koh has neither its tap ability nor its trigger.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Chrome Companion
Black Lotus
Koh, the Face Stealer
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Binding Negotiation
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Island x18

